From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:12:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/hevc: keep the hardware decoder when only the scaling
 lists of the SPS change

An SPS that comes again with the id of the active one but another content
replaces it (ff_hevc_decode_nal_sps()), and hevc_frame_start() then takes
the whole path of a new sequence: set_sps(), export_stream_params() and
get_format(), whose ff_get_format() uninitialises the hwaccel and
initialises it again. A caller that opens its own decoder again there,
such as Kodi with VA-API, shows it as a freeze of half a second to a
second and a half. The base layer of some Dolby Vision profile 7 films
switches between two SPS that differ only in their scaling lists, at IDR
pictures, several times a minute in some scenes (first reported in
CroqueMr's build, libreelec-CB1 issue 338: an AMD Radeon 780M with
VA-API).

Every hwaccel but VideoToolbox takes the scaling lists, and the flag that
enables them, with each picture (the IQ matrix buffer of VA-API,
CUVIDHEVCPICPARAMS of NVDEC, VdpPictureInfoHEVC of VDPAU,
DXVA_Qmatrix_HEVC of DXVA2, D3D11VA and D3D12VA, and the parameters that
Vulkan takes with each picture or makes again after each parameter set),
and sets nothing up from them. So when the new SPS of the base layer
differs from the active one only in scaling_list_enabled_flag,
sps_scaling_list_data_present_flag and scaling_list_data(), and one of
those hwaccels is in use, the format negotiated before and the hwaccel
are kept. Everything else is done as before: the references cleared, the
SPS of the other layers dropped, set_sps(), the stream parameters
exported, the multilayer state set up again and a new sequence for the
output. A line of AV_LOG_VERBOSE says so.

The comparison is of the parsed SPS
(ff_hevc_sps_differs_only_in_scaling_lists()): a copy of the new one
given the lists, the flag and the NAL unit of the active one must be the
same byte for byte, its VPS included, so that a difference in any other
field, also one added later, takes the old path. Without a hwaccel, with
VideoToolbox, for a layer above the base one, or when the copy cannot be
allocated, nothing changes. Upstream FFmpeg has no change for this (its
master and release branches of 2026-11-27).

Hades: tested on the host with FFmpeg's VA-API hwaccel on a VA-API driver
that decodes nothing and writes what each picture is given
(tools/regress/ffmpeg, stage slkeep): x265 streams of 8 and 10 bits whose
SPS changes only in its scaling lists, at 4 and 2 joints, call
get_format() and make the hardware decoder once instead of at each joint,
with every buffer of every picture the same as without this change, with
1 and 4 frame threads; a stream whose SPS changes in SAO, strong intra
smoothing, the latency of its DPB, its scaling lists with SAO, or its bit
depth takes the old path at each of its 5 joints; the pictures of the
software decoder are those without this change; and FATE's HEVC tests
pass. Not tested on a graphics card.
---
 libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c | 66 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 libavcodec/hevc/ps.c      | 24 ++++++++++++++
 libavcodec/hevc/ps.h      |  8 +++++
 3 files changed, 95 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c b/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
index 0cf7bc3..b45777f 100644
--- a/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
@@ -763,6 +763,52 @@ static enum AVPixelFormat get_format(HEVCContext *s, const HEVCSPS *sps)
     return 0;
 }
 
+/**
+ * Whether the hardware decoder in use takes the scaling lists of the SPS (and
+ * the flag that enables them) with each picture, and so goes on decoding a
+ * stream whose SPS changed in nothing else
+ * (ff_hevc_sps_differs_only_in_scaling_lists()): the rest of the SPS that it
+ * was set up with stays as it was.
+ */
+static int hwaccel_takes_scaling_lists(const AVCodecContext *avctx)
+{
+    if (!avctx->hwaccel || avctx->pix_fmt != avctx->hwaccel->pix_fmt)
+        return 0;
+
+    switch (avctx->hwaccel->pix_fmt) {
+    case AV_PIX_FMT_VAAPI:          // the IQ matrix buffer of vaapi_hevc_start_frame()
+    case AV_PIX_FMT_CUDA:           // CUVIDHEVCPICPARAMS of nvdec_hevc_start_frame()
+    case AV_PIX_FMT_CUARRAY:
+    case AV_PIX_FMT_VDPAU:          // VdpPictureInfoHEVC of vdpau_hevc_start_frame()
+    case AV_PIX_FMT_DXVA2_VLD:      // DXVA_Qmatrix_HEVC of dxva2_hevc_start_frame()
+    case AV_PIX_FMT_D3D11VA_VLD:
+    case AV_PIX_FMT_D3D11:
+    case AV_PIX_FMT_D3D12:          // and of d3d12va_hevc_start_frame()
+    case AV_PIX_FMT_VULKAN:         // the parameters of each picture, or session
+                                    // parameters made again after each parameter
+                                    // set (ff_vk_params_invalidate())
+        return 1;
+    default:                        // VideoToolbox: a session made from the
+                                    // parameter sets that it started with
+        return 0;
+    }
+}
+
+/**
+ * What get_format() does besides asking for a format, for a base layer whose
+ * SPS changed only in what the hardware decoder takes with each picture
+ * (hwaccel_takes_scaling_lists()): the format, the hardware decoder and its
+ * frames stay as they are.
+ */
+static int keep_format(HEVCContext *s, const HEVCSPS *sps)
+{
+    int ret = export_multilayer(s, sps->vps);
+    if (ret < 0)
+        return ret;
+
+    return setup_multilayer(s, sps->vps);
+}
+
 static int set_sps(HEVCContext *s, HEVCLayerContext *l, const HEVCSPS *sps)
 {
     int ret;
@@ -3445,6 +3491,11 @@ static int hevc_frame_start(HEVCContext *s, HEVCLayerContext *l,
     if (l->sps != sps) {
         const HEVCSPS *sps_base = s->layers[0].sps;
         enum AVPixelFormat pix_fmt = sps->pix_fmt;
+        // the SPS of the base layer changed only in its scaling lists, which
+        // the hardware decoder takes with each picture: it is kept
+        const int keep_hwaccel = l == &s->layers[0] &&
+                                 hwaccel_takes_scaling_lists(s->avctx) &&
+                                 ff_hevc_sps_differs_only_in_scaling_lists(l->sps, sps);
 
         if (l != &s->layers[0]) {
             if (!sps_base) {
@@ -3486,9 +3537,18 @@ static int hevc_frame_start(HEVCContext *s, HEVCLayerContext *l,
             return ret;
 
         if (l == &s->layers[0]) {
-            export_stream_params(s, sps);
-
-            ret = get_format(s, sps);
+            if (keep_hwaccel) {
+                const enum AVPixelFormat hw_pix_fmt = s->avctx->pix_fmt;
+
+                av_log(s->avctx, AV_LOG_VERBOSE, "SPS %u changed only in its "
+                       "scaling lists: the hardware decoder is kept\n", pps->sps_id);
+                export_stream_params(s, sps);
+                s->avctx->pix_fmt = hw_pix_fmt;
+                ret = keep_format(s, sps);
+            } else {
+                export_stream_params(s, sps);
+                ret = get_format(s, sps);
+            }
             if (ret < 0) {
                 set_sps(s, l, NULL);
                 return ret;
diff --git a/libavcodec/hevc/ps.c b/libavcodec/hevc/ps.c
index 3341458..23b4bfd 100644
--- a/libavcodec/hevc/ps.c
+++ b/libavcodec/hevc/ps.c
@@ -1732,6 +1732,30 @@ static int compare_sps(const HEVCSPS *sps1, const HEVCSPS *sps2)
            !memcmp(sps1->data, sps2->data, sps1->data_size);
 }
 
+int ff_hevc_sps_differs_only_in_scaling_lists(const HEVCSPS *ref, const HEVCSPS *sps)
+{
+    HEVCSPS *tmp;
+    int same;
+
+    if (!ref || !sps)
+        return 0;
+
+    // a copy of sps given the scaling lists and the NAL unit of ref: any other
+    // difference, also in a field added later, is then one of its bytes (both
+    // are zeroed when allocated, so their padding is too)
+    tmp = av_memdup(sps, sizeof(*sps));
+    if (!tmp)
+        return 0;
+    tmp->scaling_list_enabled = ref->scaling_list_enabled;
+    tmp->scaling_list         = ref->scaling_list;
+    tmp->data                 = ref->data;
+    tmp->data_size            = ref->data_size;
+    same = !memcmp(tmp, ref, sizeof(*ref));
+    av_free(tmp);
+
+    return same;
+}
+
 int ff_hevc_decode_nal_sps(GetBitContext *gb, AVCodecContext *avctx,
                            HEVCParamSets *ps, unsigned nuh_layer_id,
                            int apply_defdispwin)
diff --git a/libavcodec/hevc/ps.h b/libavcodec/hevc/ps.h
index f5c5f81..2afe5eb 100644
--- a/libavcodec/hevc/ps.h
+++ b/libavcodec/hevc/ps.h
@@ -526,6 +526,14 @@ int ff_hevc_parse_sps(HEVCSPS *sps, GetBitContext *gb, unsigned int *sps_id,
 
 int ff_hevc_decode_nal_vps(GetBitContext *gb, AVCodecContext *avctx,
                            HEVCParamSets *ps);
+/**
+ * Whether sps differs from ref at most in its scaling lists (the syntax
+ * elements scaling_list_enabled_flag, sps_scaling_list_data_present_flag and
+ * scaling_list_data()): every other field of the two, parsed or derived, the
+ * same byte for byte, and the same VPS. 0 when that cannot be told.
+ */
+int ff_hevc_sps_differs_only_in_scaling_lists(const HEVCSPS *ref, const HEVCSPS *sps);
+
 int ff_hevc_decode_nal_sps(GetBitContext *gb, AVCodecContext *avctx,
                            HEVCParamSets *ps, unsigned nuh_layer_id,
                            int apply_defdispwin);
